// Teleport to house (Corey, 2026-09-11). No button and no spellbook entry - the spell was
// added to the game with Construction, after 377 - but its tablet needs a recipe, and every
// other tablet reads its recipe out of magic_spell_table. So the row exists and only
// poh_tablets.rs2 asks for this id.
^teleport_to_house = 226

// Teleport to Ape Atoll. Same story as Trollheim: the button was already drawn in magic.if with
// the right level and the right rune checks - including the banana, which the client already
// counts - and only the id, the dbrow and the trigger were missing. The component was still
// carrying its unpacked name (com_569), so nothing could reference it.
^ape_atoll_teleport = 227

// Lvl-6 Enchant (Corey, 2026-09-21). Released 4 Oct 2005 with the onyx, so 377 has all of it:
// the button is drawn in magic.if at x=48 y=193 with the real checks (cosmic 1, fire 20,
// earth 20, magic > 86), the objs Ring of stone and Amulet of fury are in the cache, and so are
// the spotanim enchant_amulet2_lvl6 and the synths enchant_onyx_ring / enchant_onyx_amulet.
// Only the id, the dbrow and the trigger were missing, and the component was still carrying its
// unpacked name (com_549) so nothing could reference it. Same story as Trollheim and Ape Atoll.
// The onyx NECKLACE's enchant is not in this cache (its desc says "I wonder if this is valuable"),
// so the berserker necklace it makes was imported from OSRS: skill_magic/configs/berserker_necklace.obj.
^enchant_lvl6 = 228

// Teleother, all three (Corey, 2026-09-21). Same story as Trollheim, Ape Atoll and Lvl-6 Enchant:
// the buttons were already drawn in magic.if with buttontype=target, actiontarget=npc,player and
// the real rune and level checks, and the components were still carrying their unpacked names
// (com_511, com_521, com_541) so nothing could reference them. What genuinely did not exist was
// the accept/decline panel - except it did, four directories away, as scripts/interfaces/
// inter_251.if, now scripts/skill_magic/interfaces/teleother.if. tools/unwiredspells.json said of
// all three that "none of that exists yet"; half of that was false. FOURTH time a "does not
// exist" note has been wrong, after Trollheim, Ape Atoll and the ancient spellbook.
//
// Tele Block (com_531) STAYS in unwiredspells.json. Its note is the accurate one: it needs a
// teleport-blocked timer on the target and every teleport path in the game to honour it, which is
// a mechanism and not a panel.
^teleother_lumbridge = 229
^teleother_falador = 230
^teleother_camelot = 231
